/// Continue, checkpoint_resume and answer_guidance resume one logical Turn from retained evidence in place and never delete history: every later lane Turn and branch rooted there is preserved, and the resumed model context still reads only the lane prefix through the target. A live later Turn refuses the entire command. Internal successor execution identities fence stale writes and do not introduce a user-visible attempt or reset logical rounds. Regenerate instead clears the target's checkpoint and starts over; on a Turn that is not its lane's tail it atomically discards the later lane tail, including branches rooted there, only when discardLaterTurnIds names exactly that closure, and otherwise refuses with LaterTurnsRefusal and writes nothing.
